  {"comment": "Mortise and Tenon (mitcad#1012) with analytic volumes, on pairs of crossing boards: a rail 100 long to x = 0, 20 across and 60 high (120000), its end face side1 at x = 0, and a post 40 x 40 x 100 (160000) from x = 0 on, across the rail's end. The tenon's width runs along the end face's longest edge (the rail's height), centred. The mortise is the tenon grown by the clearance (0.1 mm) on every side and past its tip, so its volume is the tenon's plus the clearance's."},
  {"comment": "A blind tenon 40 x 8, 25 long (Box1 F1 Body1, Box2 F2 Body2, MortiseTenon1 F3): the rail gains 40 8 25 = 8000; the post loses 40.2 8.2 25.1 = 8273.964 = 8000 + 273.964 of clearance. Both bodies keep their names."},
  {"cmd": "add_feature", "def": {"type": "box", "plane": {"type": "origin", "plane": "xy"},
